  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>Account and Data Deletion</h1>
      <p>PumpSync stores minimal hosted subscription and installation metadata and does not persist Tandem credentials, Tandem tokens, raw Tandem events, or normalized Tandem samples on the backend.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="content">
        <article class="content-block">
          <h2>Effective date</h2>
          <p>Effective date: June 18, 2026</p>
          <p>Last updated: August 3, 2026</p>
        </article>

        <article class="content-block">
          <h2>Delete Tandem credentials from the device</h2>
          <p>In the PumpSync app:</p>
          <ol>
            <li>Open Settings.</li>
            <li>Open Tandem Account (in the PumpSync section).</li>
            <li>Tap Remove Credentials.</li>
          </ol>
          <p>Deleting Tandem credentials prevents future syncs until credentials are added again.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="content-block">
          <h2>Revoke Apple Health access and delete Health data</h2>
          <p>Apple Health permissions and any samples PumpSync has already written are controlled by Apple Health, not by PumpSync. Apple documents the current steps for both: see <a href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/108779" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Apple Support: view and delete Health data</a>.</p>
          <p>Deleting PumpSync does not automatically delete samples already written to Apple Health.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="content-block">
          <h2>Delete PumpSync Hosted metadata</h2>
          <p>The preferred way to request deletion is from the PumpSync app:</p>
          <ol>
            <li>Open PumpSync.</li>
            <li>Open Settings.</li>
            <li>Open Data Handling.</li>
            <li>Tap Delete Data Request.</li>
            <li>Send the prefilled email.</li>
          </ol>
          <p>The app includes the PumpSync installation ID needed to locate hosted metadata associated with that app install. Possession of the installation ID is also how deletion requests are verified; no other personal information is needed.</p>
          <p>If you plan to delete the app, copy your installation ID first. It is stored only on that device and cannot be recovered after the app is deleted.</p>
          <p>If you cannot send the request from the app, email <a href="mailto:support@ericslutz.dev?subject=DELETION%20REQUEST%20-%20PumpSync%20Support">support@ericslutz.dev</a> with the subject <strong>DELETION REQUEST - PumpSync Support</strong>.</p>
          <p>Include your PumpSync installation ID. To find it in the app, open Settings, then Developer, then copy the Installation ID.</p>
          <p>If you already deleted the app and no longer have the installation ID, email the same address anyway. Hosted metadata can be located from App Store subscription records where possible, and requests without an ID are handled on a best-effort basis.</p>
          <p>{{ claims.doNotSend }}</p>
          <p>Deletion covers PumpSync hosted server-side metadata associated with the subscription or installation, subject to records PumpSync must retain for security, fraud prevention, legal compliance, billing, dispute handling, or service integrity.</p>
          <p>Hosted server-side metadata means the records listed in the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy's</a> Backend storage section: subscription entitlement state, installation mappings, rate-limit events, sync attempt metadata, idempotency records, and redacted operational audit events.</p>
          <p>Deletion requests are processed within 30 days, and you will receive a reply confirming when deletion is complete.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="content-block">
          <h2>Subscription billing is separate</h2>
          <p>Requesting data deletion or deleting the app does not cancel a PumpSync Hosted subscription.</p>
          <p>Manage or cancel the subscription in your device's subscription settings or through <a href="https://support.apple.com/HT202039" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Apple's manage-subscriptions guide</a>.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="content-block">
          <h2>Self-hosted users</h2>
